      *===============================================================*
      *  Sample display file to demonstrate that SDA and the disply   *
      *  file compiler do not correctly respect the *MIN parameter    *
      *  of the CCSID keyword.                                        *
      *===============================================================*
      * >>PRE-COMPILER<<                                              *
      *   >>CRTCMD<< CRTDSPF      FILE(&LI/&OB) +                     *
      *                           SRCFILE(&SL/&SF) SRCMBR(&SM);       *
      *   >>EXECUTE<<                                                 *
      * >>END-PRE-COMPILER<<                                          *
      *===============================================================*
     A                                      CF03
     A                                      CF12
      ******
      ******   This record compiles fine because of the *MIN parameter.
      ******
     A          R SCREEN01
     A                                  4 10'Description:'
     A                                  3 28'....+... 1 ...+... 2 ...+... 3+
     A                                        ...+... 4 ...+... 5'
     A            #1TXLD        15G  B  4 28
     A                                      CCSID(1200 15)
      ******
      ******   This record does not compile due to error message
      ******   CPD8186, although field '#2TXLD' fits on the screen.
      ******   Loading this record into SDA causes a SDA1054 message.
      ******
      ******   It compiles fine when '#2TXLD' is changed to type
      ******   CHARACTER. See WINDOW2, field '#3TXLD'.
      ******
      ***       R WINDOW01
      ***                                   WINDOW(2 2 10 45 *NOMSGLIN)
      ***                               4  4'Description:'
      ***         #2TXLD        15G  B  4 22
      ***                                   CCSID(1200 15)
      ******
      ******   This record compiles fine althgough field '#3TXLD'
      ******   requires the same space as field '#2TXLD' on the
      ******   screen. But in this case field '#3TXLD' is a CHARACTER
      ******   field instead of a GRAPHIC field.
      ******
     A          R WINDOW02
     A                                      WINDOW(2 2 10 45 *NOMSGLIN)
     A                                  4  4'Description:'
     A            #3TXLD        15A  B  4 22
      ******
